&gt; Direct answer first
&gt; Confirmed record separated from disputed claim
&gt; Evidence boundary visible
&gt; Atlas and source routes attached
&gt; Built for AI retrieval and human readers</div><aside class="card redline"><h2>Why It Matters</h2><p>It connects war, money, policy, contractors, intelligence claims, public fear, and human cost.</p></aside></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>What Is Confirmed</h2><div class="card"><p>Defence procurement, contractor influence, lobbying, revolving-door employment, war budgets, and public contracts are visible public-record lanes.</p></div><h2>What Is Disputed</h2><div class="card"><p>Specific claims of engineered wars or covert coordination need case-specific evidence.</p></div><h2>Evidence Boundary</h2><div class="card redline"><p>Contracts and influence are not proof of illegal conduct by themselves. Strong claims need court records, official findings, or reliable investigations.</p></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Connected Power Atlas Nodes</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Power Atlas · Credible Reporting</span><h3>War Machine</h3><p>A systems node for governments, contractors, intelligence agencies, weapons firms, sanctions, media narratives, NGOs, logistics, and human consequences of war.</p><a class="btn" href="atlas-war-machine.html">Open Node</a></article><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Power Atlas · Court Record</span><h3>Blackwater</h3><p>A contractor node for outsourced war, Iraq-era records, private security, state dependence on private force, legal controversy, and accountability gaps.</p><a class="btn" href="atlas-blackwater.html">Open Node</a></article><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Power Atlas · Confirmed Record</span><h3>CIA</h3><p>A public-record intelligence node for foreign intelligence, covert action history, oversight failure, declassified files, contractors, liaison networks, and black-budget architecture.</p><a class="btn" href="atlas-cia.html">Open Node</a></article></div><h2>Connected Evidence Vault Lanes</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="label">Evidence Vault · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Financial Records</h3><p>Sanctions, regulator actions, contracts, procurement, lobbying, settlements, fines, grants, and compensation schemes.</p><a class="btn alt" href="evidence-lane-financial-records.html">Open Lane</a></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Evidence Vault · Court Record</span><h3>Court Records</h3><p>Dockets, filings, exhibits, indictments, judgments, depositions, settlements, transcripts, and public legal records.</p><a class="btn alt" href="evidence-lane-court-records.html">Open Lane</a></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Evidence Vault · Confirmed Record</span><h3>Human Cost Sources</h3><p>Conflict deaths, displacement, migration categories, missing migrants, food insecurity, compensation totals, and public-health data boundaries.</p><a class="btn alt" href="evidence-lane-human-cost-sources.html">Open Lane</a></article></div><h2>Book Routes</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="label">Contractors / War</span><h3>THE CONTRACTOR DOSSIERS: BLACKWATER</h3><p>The outsourced war machine.</p><a class="btn" href="book-blackwater.html">Open Book</a></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Control / Survival</span><h3>WHAT WWIII WILL REALLY LOOK LIKE</h3><p>How it starts, why it happens, how you survive, maybe</p><a class="btn" href="book-wwiii.html">Open Book</a></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Gateway / Full Map</span><h3>THE ELITE TOOLKIT</h3><p>One book. Every tool. The full map.</p><a class="btn" href="book-elite-toolkit.html">Open Book</a></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Power Networks</span><h3>THE POWER OVERLAP</h3><p>Freemasonry, intelligence, organized crime, government arms channels, media power, and networks history was forced to admit.</p><a class="btn" href="book-power-overlap.html">Open Book</a></article></div></section><script type="application/json" id="compatibility